<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Olive Grove of Koundouros</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1205">1205</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Olive Grove of Koundouros was fought in Messenia in the south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> in 1205. A small force of crusaders under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-of-champlitte">William of Champlitte</a> and Geoffrey of Villehardouin, put at a few hundred knights and men by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-the-morea">Chronicle of the Morea</a>, defeated a much larger army of local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>. The victory opened the way for the conquest of the western Peloponnese and the founding of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-olive-grove-of-koundouros.jpg" alt="Battle of the Olive Grove of Koundouros" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olivenhain.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
